  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">IGAD 2023-2026 Institutional Gender Capacity Building</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">IGAD Internal Gender Capacity building</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Ambassaden mottog ett projektf&#xf6;rslag fr&#xe5;n IGAD:s j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetssavdelning i oktober 2022. Det f&#xf6;reslagna programmet syftar till att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra IGAD:s institutionella kapacitet f&#xf6;r j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsintegrering. Projektet kommer att anv&#xe4;nda digitala och andra verktyg f&#xf6;r att &#xf6;ka medvetenheten och m&#xe4;tbarheten kring j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsintegrering inom IGAD:S olika typer av interventioner. L&#xe4;rdomarna fr&#xe5;n projektet f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntas sedan kunna anv&#xe4;ndas i sambarbetet  andra REC:s som Sverige ger st&#xf6;d till. Projektet planeras att p&#xe5;g&#xe5; i tre &#xe5;r, fr&#xe5;n juli 2023 till juni 2026, med en total budget om 21 MSEK. 
Projektets &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att skapa institutionella metoder som &#xe4;r fira fr&#xe5;n diskriminerande f&#xf6;rdomar och stereotyper och som kan anv&#xe4;ndas inom IGAD och dess olika programverksamheter. M&#xe5;let &#xe4;r vidare att &#xf6;ka IGAD:s institutionella kapacitet n&#xe4;r det g&#xe4;ller systemuppbyggnad, att bidra till den interna f&#xf6;rst&#xe5;elsen av j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsfr&#xe5;gor, och att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhetsintegreringen inom IGAD:s egna program.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Embassy received a request for support from IGAD&#x2019;s gender affairs department in October 2022. The proposed program aims to enhance IGAD Institutional capacity of gender mainstreaming and attaining gender equality. The project will use key digital elements, awareness raising mechanisms and tools that increase accountability of all IGAD divisions to enable attaining better gender related results of other interventions of IGAD. The learning from this intervention is expected to be mainstreamed to other RECs that are supported by Sweden. The total budget of the project is 21 MSEK for the period of three years, from July 2023 to June 2026.
The goal of the program is to create gender equitable institutional practices that are free from gender related biases and stereotyping in IGAD and IGAD program interventions as an organization and at member States level to effectively address gender inequality. The overall objective of this intervention is to enhance institutional capacity of IGAD in terms of system building and staff awareness raising and improving gender mainstreaming across IGAD programs.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Objective of the intervention

The IGAD project on Institutional Capacity Strengthening of IGAD on Gender Equality and Women Empowerment (GEWE) is designed with a premise that institutional capacity building will lead to organizational transformation and gender responsiveness.

The project has the following two overarching and interrelated outcomes:

1. System, clear approach, and strategy in place in IGAD Secretariat and specialized offices for result and evidence-based gender equality and women empowerment interventions.

2. Systematic coordination and gender equitable organizational culture among IGAD divisions in place for promoting the IGAD Gender Equality agenda in an effective and sustainable manner.

The two outcomes were intended to be achieved through four key outputs which were:

1.1. Increased capacity of IGAD to implement the Regional Gender Strategy:

1.2.: Increased capacity of IGAD Secretariat and specialized office sub offices to promote Gender equality institutionally and in programme intervention

1.3: Regional gender transformative Leadership Academy and Gender Knowledge hub established.

2.1: Increased capacity of IGAD on coordination, gender equitable organizational culture and gender management systems</narrative>
  </description>
